{"parentUuid":"bb08d513-54e2-44f5-81cc-bc5a063b9dad","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"064cefd4-6e96-476e-8934-d2b8ef3002b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"但是实际上其不是包裹，只是加上头解析的时候，从头解析吧"},"uuid":"b3bec49a-ec3f-4417-aeef-bb787adaae60","timestamp":"2026-07-04T02:49:15.781Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\project\\easyTalk\\网络知识","sessionId":"21ff3827-8b2e-434a-b620-a49c88bce92c","version":"2.1.160","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"b3bec49a-ec3f-4417-aeef-bb787adaae60","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_1bf3d1863a774dbfbbb56f3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is making a very insightful correction. They're saying that the Ethernet frame isn't actually like nested envelopes/packages where things are physically \"wrapped\" inside each other. Instead, when data is sent, headers are simply added to the front (and trailer to the end), and when received, the headers are stripped off from the front sequentially.\n\nThe user is pointing out that my \"nested envelope\" analogy, while helpful conceptually, isn't physically accurate. The actual data structure is just a long flat sequence of bytes - header after header is prepended, and during parsing, headers are removed from the front one by one.\n\nLet me clarify this in simple terms.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"33a0b014-4bf0-408a-81d4-4e28eb8b22d3","timestamp":"2026-07-04T02:49:20.030Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\project\\easyTalk\\网络知识","sessionId":"21ff3827-8b2e-434a-b620-a49c88bce92c","version":"2.1.160","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"33a0b014-4bf0-408a-81d4-4e28eb8b22d3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_1bf3d1863a774dbfbbb56f3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 你说得完全对，不是真的\"套娃\"\n\n我之前的比喻容易让人误以为里面真的有好几层信封套在一起。实际上：\n\n---\n\n### 发送时：就是在前面不断贴标签\n\n```\n\"给我百度首页\"\n```\n\nTCP 层说：我在前面加一段信息\n\n```\n[TCP头] + \"给我百度首页\"\n```\n\nIP 层说：我再往前面加一段\n\n```\n[IP头] + [TCP头] + \"给我百度首页\"\n```\n\n以太网层说：我再往最前面加一段，最后面加个尾巴\n\n```\n[以太网头] + [IP头] + [TCP头] + \"给我百度首页\" + [FCS]\n```\n\n**就是这样，一条直线，从左到右，不断往前面贴标签。** 没有什么信封套信封，就是一长串数据，前面加了三段说明信息，后面加了一段校验码。\n\n---\n\n### 接收时：就是从头开始，一层层撕掉\n\n交换机收到这一长串数据：\n\n```\n[以太网头] + [IP头] + [TCP头] + \"给我百度首页\" + [FCS]\n```\n\n交换机只看最前面那一段（以太网头），看完之后原封不动把整个数据转发走，**不撕**。\n\n路由器收到后，**撕掉最前面的以太网头**：\n\n```\n[IP头] + [TCP头] + \"给我百度首页\" + [FCS]\n```\n\n路由器看最前面的 IP 头，看完后处理完，再给这个数据加上新的以太网头发出去。\n\n你的电脑收到后，**先撕以太网头，再撕 IP 头，再撕 TCP 头**：\n\n```\n第1步：看 [以太网头] → 撕掉\n第2步：看 [IP头] → 撕掉\n第3步：看 [TCP头] → 撕掉\n第4步：剩下 → \"给我百度首页\"\n```\n\n**就是从左到右，一段段撕掉，最后拿到最右边的真正内容。**\n\n---\n\n### 用大白话说\n\n- **发送**：写好内容 → 前面贴 TCP 标签 → 前面贴 IP 标签 → 前面贴以太网标签\n- **接收**：看最前面的标签 → 撕掉 → 看下一个标签 → 撕掉 → 最后拿到内容\n\n**就是一条直线上不断加标签、撕标签的过程。** 不是套娃，是排队。前面的标签先加后撕，后面的标签后加先撕。\n\n---\n\n之前的套娃比喻是为了帮你理解\"每层都把上面所有东西包进去\"这个概念，但物理上确实不是套在一起的，就是一长串字节，前面加头部、后面加尾巴。\n\n感谢你指出来，你理解得很到位。"}],"usage":{"input_tokens":797,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":33088,"output_tokens":782,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"d08bfb42-7edb-4047-a6fb-f3cfe70474fe","timestamp":"2026-07-04T02:49:30.549Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\project\\easyTalk\\网络知识","sessionId":"21ff3827-8b2e-434a-b620-a49c88bce92c","version":"2.1.160","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
